star trek picard keeps serving up easter  eggs for longtime trek fans from nods to  picard and worf's family histories to a  notable figure from the original series  it also has brent spiner playing yet  another character in a star trek show  here's all the references you may have  missed  in the fifth episode of season two we  finally learn more about what the crew  must do to get back to 2024 and the  reason for the divergence in the  timeline we learned that the woman  reading a dixon hill novel in the  previous episode wasn't just a random  passerby she's renee picard an important  thread in the tapestry of history and a  key figure in the family tree of  jean-luc picard she is the lead  astronaut for the upcoming europa  mission which we now know is more than a  simple easter egg referencing the series  fictional history of space flight it is  also a critical moment in the  development of earth toward their  brighter future renee picard also fits  in nicely to what we know of picard's  ancestors in the tng episode family we  met his brother and nephew and it was  said that picard's exploration of space  went against the family's tradition we  know from the episode journey's end that  he was descended from a 17th century  spanish soldier javier maribona picard  while a later picard fought for the  french at the battle of trafalgar in the  film star trek nemesis picard looked  back at his family history and noted  there weren't many picards who were  explorers he was one of the few who was  i was the first picard to leave our  solar system  it caused quite a stir in the family it  would seem that renee picard who shares  a first name with john luke's male  nephew renee seems to fit in perfectly  on the picard family tree while she is  apparently one of the rare explorers  that captain picard mentioned it seems  her exploration will be limited to our  own solar system  since arriving in the 21st century  picard and the crew of the la serena  have been seeking a mysterious being  called the watcher after gainan leads  picard to her doorstep were finally  introduced to a woman who somehow bears  the likeness of picard's romulan  companion larys but this is not lyris as  the watcher who introduces herself as  tallinn seems as mystified as we are by  the resemblance instead she describes  herself as a supervisor of earthly  events she has been assigned the task of  watching over historical events and  monitoring the destiny of renee picard  in particular who she describes as a  single thread of the tapestry of history  picard recognizes tallinn's  self-description right away recalling a  similar human who was once encountered  by kirk's enterprise  gary seven he too was recruited by  superior beings as an agent who would in  your words protect the tapestry of  history this is the season's second  reference to kirk's adventures on the  enterprise this time a nod to the  episode assignment earth the episode saw  kirk and crew travel back to 1968 where  they met a man called gary 7 who also  called himself supervisor tasked with  completing another agent's mission to  ensure that humans did not annihilate  each other in nuclear war with the  revelation of the watcher as one of gary  seven's people we now know that the  supervisors do more than just help  mankind on a broad historical level they  are also on earth to watch over and  protect important individuals whose  lives could impact the earth's destiny  we had heard that actor brent spiner  would be reappearing in season 2 even  before it began but some fans had  assumed that he would be reprising his  role from season 1 as alton in a gosun  the son of data's creator nunian tsum  instead he plays someone from much  earlier adam soon one of the scientists  ancestors  we saw a glimpse of him in the dark  future with a holographic monument to a  man named adam soon who preached that a  safe galaxy is a human galaxy now we  meet adam soon in the flesh who is not a  man far from the future but rather our  present in 2024 the ancestor of noon and  soon is a scientist and geneticist  apparently looking for a cure for his  daughter played by issa briones this  human daughter suffers from a rare  condition that makes sunlight fatal to  her in this episode sung is a leading  geneticist with delusions of curing all  of the world's diseases with his  research into eugenics this meshes with  the universe's fictional history  specifically the aftermath of the 1990s  eugenics wars this also tracks with what  we know of the zooms and like renee  picard adam soon fits perfectly within  the soon family tree on star trek  enterprise set less than 150 years into  adam soon's future his descendant  ericsson is a brilliant genetic  researcher a mad scientist who  genetically altered embryos to become  human super soldiers it would seem now  that the soon family's obsession with  improving humanity stretched further  back than we ever suspected ultimately  this soon has his medical license  revoked for a number of ethical  violations  adam soon's work in eugenics leads to a  number of important breakthroughs but it  hasn't been without its controversy  either having apparently experimented on  ex-soldiers through a private contractor  he's been brought before a medical  review board to explain himself among  the panelists however is a man with a  surname that fans of the next generation  should know well the dark-haired man  sits silently with a cold stare and his  name plate reads vasily regenco vice  chair this cannot be anything other than  an easter egg referencing tng's  lieutenant wharf the orphaned klingon  officer after being found by humans the  site of the kittimer massacre as a child  dwarf was raised by human foster parents  on earth a kind russian couple named  sergey and helena regenko  sergey of course appeared in the episode  family mostly a story about jean-luc  picard returning to france but in the b  story dwarf has a reunion with his earth  parents too we learned that sergey was  an enlisted starfleet crewman aboard the  uss intrepid and after marrying helena  they had one biological son nikolai who  was played by paul cervino in the  episode homeward later wharf's son  alexander would take the roshenko  surname as well little else was revealed  about the rajenko family on tng but here  we learn they have a rich family history  with vasily being an important figure in  the world's medical community in 2024  vasily roshenko wasn't the only easter  egg on the medical review board though  the panel's chairman is a woman named  diane werner and her appearance is a  clever nod to the series time travel  routes not just any guest star the woman  who plays werner is an actress with some  experience in time travel shenanigans  herself she also happens to be the woman  who directed the episode and the episode  prior leah thompson science fiction fans  will know the name from the 1980s time  travel trilogy back to the future where  thompson played marty mcfly's mother  lorraine mcfly  you know what i do in those situations  what  i don't worry  with episodes of star trek picard under  her belt she's re-entered the world of  science fiction on the other side of the  camera this time a perfect fit for the  woman who starred opposite michael j fox  in one of the most celebrated time  travel classics  now that picard has discovered the  watcher and learned just who and what  their mission to restore history  involves he gathers the lacirana crew to  go over a plan of action some including  rios are perplexed at how rene picard a  single woman could be so crucial to  history that she's the difference  between a bright and hopeful future and  a dark totalitarian nightmare reality  picard says he's not sure how or why his  ancestor is so important either but he  knows there's a reason why she's  apparently so unknown as he reminds the  crew the history of this time period is  wildly incomplete the century leading up  to first contact was just rife with  chaos and picard would know as this is a  clear reference to the events he took  part in during the film star trek first  contact another time travel story that  saw the enterprise go back to 2063 just  39 years after this episode is set in  that time it's said that the earth was  still recovering from the third world  war and most records of the era were  lost or incomplete here all picard  claims to know of his ancestor is that  she commanded the europa mission and  that while exploring the solar system it  was said that she discovered a  microorganism that she believed was  sentient clearly this is a hint of  things to come in the second half of  season two but if track history is  anything to go by it sounds like records  of the day will be lost during a major  global catastrophe  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

